<title>UK: No injuries at Albright's factory fire.</title>
<headline>No injuries at Albright's factory fire.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Albright &amp; Wilson Plc said there were no injuries at its UK chemical factory fire this morning and all personnel had been accounted for.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the fire was under control but continued to burn, generating black smoke, and the public had been advised to stay indoors until further notice.  </p>
<p>Albright &amp; Wilson said a thorough investigation would start as soon as the fire had been brought completely under control.</p>
<p>The blast happened at 0930 GMT this morning at the company's Avonmouth Works, near Bristol in western England.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
